{"abstract":"Exploring Unprecedented Extremes What: Facing the urgent challenge of extreme weather and climate-related events, our societal frameworks for “resilience” and “adaptation” are proving to be insufficient. This paper introduces the “Exploring Unprecedented Extremes” workshop, which was convened to elucidate the research gap in light of such challenges. The workshop tackled a broad spectrum of issues, ranging from assessing out-of-sample climatic events that defy traditional modeling approaches to enhancing the communication of risks and likelihoods associated with such unprecedented events.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Matte, Dominic","Christensen, Jens H.","Drews, Martin","Sobolowski, Stefan","Paquin, Dominique","Lynch, Amanda","Bremer, Scott","Engholm, Ida","Brunet, Nicolas D.","Kolstad, Erik W.","Kettleborough, Helena","Thompson, Vikki","Bevacqua, Emanuele","Heinrich, Dorothy","Pryor, Sara C.","Böhnisch, Andrea","Feser, Frauke","Prein, Andreas F.","Fischer, Erich","Leduc, Martin"],"cuid":["S03-092.69-761671"],"event":{"end":"2023-11-23","place":"Montréal, ca","start":"2023-11-21","title":"Exploring Unprecedented Extremes","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Matte, Dominic"],"country":["Canada","Germany","Netherlands","Norway","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bjerknes Centre for Climate Research","Brown University","Cornell University","ETH Zürich","Helmholtz Centre for Environmental Research","Helmholtz-Zentrum Hereon","Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","Manchester Metropolitan University","National Center for Atmospheric Research","Ouranos","Red Cross Red Crescent Climate Centre","Royal Netherlands Meteorological Institute","Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Zurich","University of Bergen","University of Guelph","University of Manchester","University of Rhode Island"],"keyword":["Atmosphere","Climate change","Climate models","Extreme events","Social science"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-RDKA"],"OT":["Ouranos, Montréal, Québec, Canada;"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-RDKA","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how to engage and adapt to unprecedented extremes","src":["arkc","dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-ART-RDKA","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1175/BAMS-D-24-0138.1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-092.69-761671","identifier":[{"id":"85202295095","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["arkc-4924a6cd-9dd6-4321-a758-052e4ce205c1","dtu-5c730ad0-6041-49fd-a46b-1d435973efe2","ku-d4f338cf-013b-4167-ac15-4faee8204e2b"],"keyword":["Atmosphere","Climate change","Climate models","Extreme events","No","Social Science"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-5F7D202199B638EA99DE21789B79D5D9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1175/BAMS-D-24-0138.1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/377460772/bams-BAMS-D-24-0138.1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/402758648/bams_BAMS_D_24_0138.1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ca","key":"ouranos","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Ouranos","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar"