:"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hannah","key":"zuckermanhannahpau","last":"Zuckerman","name":"Zuckerman, Hannah","rank":1577,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ran","key":"lyuranpau","last":"Lyu","name":"Lyu, Ran","rank":1578,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wayne","key":"pullanwaynepau","last":"Pullan","name":"Pullan, Wayne","rank":1579,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33326193"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/database/baz085","issn":["17580463"],"journal":"Database: The Journal of Biological Databases and Curation","pages":"1-67","paperid":"085","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Database: The Journal of Biological Databases and Curation","title_org":"Database","volume":"2019"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85082592913"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-88b053a3-63ab-4380-ab20-90a54b540224","au-6bf5b1c8-6cc1-4ee4-b711-48f478a90279","ku-291608f7-132f-41ac-94ae-fe9aa192baf0","sdu-a9479d7b-e13c-4f9b-8edd-dd71403513e8"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Large expert-curated database for benchmarking document similarity detection in biomedical literature search","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-087.05-006608","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Primary liver cancer (PLC) ranks among the most lethal solid cancers worldwide due to lack of effective biomarkers for early detection and limited treatment options in advanced stages. Development of primary culture models that closely recapitulate phenotypic and molecular diversities of PLC is urgently needed to improve the patient outcome. Long-term cultures of 7 primary liver cancer cell lines of hepatocellular and cholangiocellular origin were established using defined culture conditions. Morphological and histological characteristics of obtained cell lines and xenograft tumors were analyzed and compared to original tumors. Time course analyses of transcriptomic and genomic changes were performed using next-generation sequencing (NGS). Key oncogenic alterations were identified by targeted NGS and cell lines carrying potentially actionable mutations were treated with corresponding specific inhibitors. PDCL fully resembled morphological features of the primary cancers in vitro and in vivo over extended period in culture. Genomic alterations as well as transcriptome profiles showed high similarity with primary tumors and remained stable during long-term culturing. Targeted-NGS confirmed that key oncogenic mutations such as TP53, KRAS, CTNNB1 as well as actionable mutations (e.g. MET, cKIT, KDR) were highly conserved in PDCL and amenable for individualized therapeutic approaches. Integrative genomic and transcriptomic approaches further demonstrated that PDCL more closely resemble molecular and prognostic features of PLC than established cell lines and are valuable tool for direct target evaluation. Our integrative analysis demonstrates that PDCL represents refined model for discovery of relevant molecular subgroups and exploration of precision medicine approaches for the treatment of this deadly disease. This article is protected by copyright. All rights reserved.","author_count":23,"contributors":["Castven, Darko","Becker, Diana","Czauderna, Carolin","Wilhelm, Diana","Andersen, Jesper B","Strand, Susanne","Hartmann, Monika","Heilmann-Heimbach, Stefanie","Roth, Wilfried","Hartmann, Nils","Straub, Beate K","Mahn, Friederike L","Franck, Sophia","Pereira, Sharon","Haupts, Anna","Vogel, Arndt","Wörns, Marcus A","Weinmann, Arndt","Heinrich, Stefan","Lang, Hauke","Thorgeirsson, Snorri S","Galle, Peter R","Marquardt, Jens U"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-412326"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"application of patient derived liver cancer cells for phenotypic characterization and therapeutic target identification","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-412326","identifier":[{"id":"30485423","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85058615104","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-1fb6fd57-eb9b-436b-bf53-c1ab0cf4a0db"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-33D101E0BE35CF250F09158AB732C52D"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, BRIC, Andersen Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Darko","key":"castvendarkopau","last":"Castven","name":"Castven, Darko","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Diana","key":"beckerdianapau","last":"Becker","name":"Becker, Diana","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Carolin","key":"czaudernacarolinpau","last":"Czaud