twork/European Heart Rhythm Association consensus conference","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-091.23-027780","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: To assess the 12-month efficacy and safety profile of an individualized regimen of ranibizumab 0.5 mg driven by stabilization criteria in patients with macular edema secondary to central retinal vein occlusion (CRVO). DESIGN: A 24-month, prospective, open-label, single-arm, multicenter study. PARTICIPANTS: Three hundred fifty-seven patients. METHODS: Patients were treated with monthly ranibizumab 0.5-mg injections (minimum of 3 injections) until stable visual acuity (VA) was maintained for 3 consecutive months. Thereafter, ranibizumab 0.5 mg was dosed as needed if monthly monitoring indicated a loss of VA resulting from disease activity. MAIN OUTCOME MEASURES: Mean change from baseline at month 12 in best-corrected VA (BCVA; primary end point) and safety over 12 months. The efficacy of this regimen in subgroups categorized by baseline BCVA score, CRVO duration, or presence of macular ischemia (exploratory analysis). RESULTS: At baseline, the mean BCVA was 53.0 letters and mean CRVO duration was 8.9 months (median, 2.4 months). Ranibizumab 0.5-mg treatment resulted in a statistically significant mean gain in BCVA from baseline at month 12 of 12.3 letters (standard deviation [SD], 16.72 letters; P < 0.0001). The mean number of ranibizumab injections up to month 12 was 8.1 (SD, 2.77). At month 12, mean BCVA gains were similar with or without macular ischemia at baseline (11.6 vs. 12.1 letters); the mean BCVA gain was higher with baseline CRVO duration of less than 3 months (13.4 letters) than with a longer duration (≥3-<9 months, 11.1 letters; ≥9 months, 10.9 letters). Patients with lower baseline BCVA had larger mean BCVA gains at month 12 than those with higher baseline BCVA (≤39/40-59/≥60 and 18.0/12.7/8.9 letters, respectively), although the absolute BCVA at month 12 was higher with higher baseline BCVA. No new ocular or nonocular safety events were observed. CONCLUSIONS: An individualized dosing regimen of ranibizumab 0.5 mg driven by stabilization criteria for up to 12 months resulted in significant BCVA gain in a broad population of patients with macular edema secondary to CRVO, including those with macular ischemia at baseline. The safety findings were consistent with those reported in previous ranibizumab studies in patients with CRVO.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Larsen, Michael","Waldstein, Sebastian M","Boscia, Francesco","Gerding, Heinrich","Monés, Jordi","Tadayoni, Ramin","Priglinger, Siegfried","Wenzel, Andreas","Barnes, Elizabeth","Pilz, Stefan","Stubbings, William","Pearce, Ian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-416587"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corpau":["CRYSTAL Study Group"],"country":["Austria","France","Germany","Italy","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Liverpool University Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","Medical University of Vienna","Novartis","Paris-Cité University","University of Münster","University of Sassari"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Institut de la Màcula, Centro Médico Teknon, and Barcelona Macula Foundation, Barcelona, Spain."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"individualized ranibizumab regimen driven by stabilization criteria for central retinal vein occlusion twelve month results of the crystal study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ophtha.2016.01.011","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-416587","identifier":[{"id":"26896124","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84958214819","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-26af9bcc-434c-4608-8f69-2d605b4cc73f"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-156419BB8EAFD2F1B801ABBC3B8EDD6B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ophtha.2016.01.011","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"at","key":"medical university of vienna","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Medical University of Vienna","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"university of sassari","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Sassari","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"university of münster","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Münster","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Institut de la Màcula, Centro Médico Teknon, and Barcelona Macula Foundation, Barcelona, Spain."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"fr","key":"paris cité university","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Paris-Cité University","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"de","key":"ludwig maximilian university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"ch","key":"novartis","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Novartis","used":1}